WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.279 --> 00:00:03.669
There was nothing out of the ordinary about
Timmy Mason.

00:00:03.669 --> 00:00:07.660
Like a lot of healthy, eight-year-old boys,
Timmy liked to go on little adventures in

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:12.230
and around his neighborhood, and now that
Summer vacation had finally rolled around,

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:15.420
he had more time than ever to explore.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:20.940
But during one particularly hot day, Timmy
suddenly realized that he was exhausted.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:24.710
The heat was beginning to get to him, and
he’d forgotten to pack a water bottle.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:29.970
All he had was a couple dollars and a handful
of quarters rattling around in his pocket.

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:34.219
He was considering heading to a nearby corner
store and purchasing a drink, when he first

00:00:34.219 --> 00:00:35.930
heard the music.

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:40.629
It was a tinny rendition of “Pop Goes The
Weasel”, playing in the distance, underscored

00:00:40.629 --> 00:00:42.680
by the rumbling of an engine.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.640
Timmy’s face lit up; this could only mean
one thing.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:49.089
An ice cream truck, just in time.

00:00:49.089 --> 00:00:53.589
He ran in the direction of the sounds, not
wanting to miss out on the cool, sweet relief

00:00:53.589 --> 00:00:55.149
from the intense Summer heat.

00:00:55.149 --> 00:00:59.969
But when the ice cream truck suddenly rounded
a corner and came into view, Timmy felt a

00:00:59.969 --> 00:01:01.329
pang of anxiety.

00:01:01.329 --> 00:01:05.500
It didn’t look like most of the ice cream
trucks he’d seen driving around his neighborhood

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.030
in prior Summers.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:11.670
It was shoddy - an older, more boxy model
with peeling, white paint.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:16.520
But it was so hot out that Timmy felt he couldn’t
afford to be picky if he wanted to cool off.

00:01:16.520 --> 00:01:20.840
The ice cream truck came to a noisy stop,
and Timmy ran over.

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:25.000
When he reached the side of the truck, he
noticed some other strange details: There

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.500
was no serving hatch in the back of the truck.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:32.410
The closest thing was a thin, dark groove
cut into the driver’s side door - a door

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:36.390
that seemed almost drawn onto the side of
the truck, rather than a door that looked

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:38.480
like it could actually open.

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:40.070
How could the driver even get in?

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:43.700
And adding to the strangeness, there was no
menu on the truck, either.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:47.659
Typically, on your friendly neighborhood ice
cream truck, you’d find a colorful collection

00:01:47.659 --> 00:01:52.260
of all the frozen treats you could buy, along
with how much they’d cost you.

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:53.479
But not here.

00:01:53.479 --> 00:01:54.899
Timmy gulped nervously.

00:01:54.899 --> 00:01:59.869
He knew something was wrong here, but for
some reason, he couldn’t seem to pull himself

00:01:59.869 --> 00:02:00.869
away.

00:02:00.869 --> 00:02:03.900
He cleared his throat, forced a polite smile,
and said:

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.750
“Can I get a green popsicle, please?”

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:08.970
There was a strange rumbling noise inside
the ice cream truck.

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:14.360
Suddenly, the slot in the door opened a little
wider, and a long, green popsicle in a plastic

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:15.780
wrapper emerged.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:20.970
It came with a small piece of paper, with
“$5.75” in loose, scratchy handwriting

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:21.970
on it.

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:25.280
Timmy regarded the note with suspicion, and
then said that he was sorry, but he didn’t

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:28.480
have $5.75.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:30.640
Something inside the truck began rumbling
again.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:33.530
Louder this time; more aggressive.

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:38.260
While the truck growled from within, Timmy
noticed something else was wrong.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:44.209
His popsicle was no ordinary popsicle: It
was a dead snake, straightened out and frozen

00:02:44.209 --> 00:02:45.209
solid.

00:02:45.209 --> 00:02:47.849
Timmy screamed and dropped the so-called popsicle.

00:02:47.849 --> 00:02:51.150
He turned, and began to run, but it was already
too late.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:56.110
The slot behind him yawned open fully, and
a rusty, spring-loaded chain fired out like

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:57.319
a harpoon.

00:02:57.319 --> 00:03:02.160
On the end of this chain was a large, snapping
bear trap, which quickly latched onto Timmy’s

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:03.160
left leg.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:07.340
The chain yanked and pulled him backwards,
dragging him ever closer to the darkened crevice

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:08.800
in the truck’s door.

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:13.170
Moments later, he was pulled inside, and the
hatch closed behind him.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:18.370
His screams were muffled, and then overpowered
entirely by the rumbling within.

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:23.830
Soon after, there was silence, and finally,
the cheerful tune of “Pop Goes The Weasel”

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:25.909
began to play once more.

00:03:25.909 --> 00:03:32.470
The truck drove away, prepared to serve its
frozen delights to another child somewhere.

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:36.819
Not long after Timmy was reported missing,
another young boy bought a scoop of strawberry

00:03:36.819 --> 00:03:39.890
ice cream in a waffle cone from the same truck.

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:44.150
The boy’s mother was horrified to find that
this alleged ice cream was full of what seemed

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:46.209
like blood and raw meat.

00:03:46.209 --> 00:03:52.010
Lab tests later confirmed that this gory ice
cream was a perfect genetic match for poor,

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:53.349
missing Timmy Mason.

00:03:53.349 --> 00:03:58.629
It didn’t take long for the SCP Foundation
to get involved, seeing as mysterious, horrifying

00:03:58.629 --> 00:04:03.260
deaths like this were often the first sign
of an anomaly’s presence in the area, and

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:07.620
they were able to quickly track down and isolate
the rogue ice cream truck.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:11.590
This wasn’t especially difficult for the
agents assigned to the case, since it literally

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:14.680
announced its presence with loud, obnoxious
music.

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:21.690
While it was easy to find, the ice cream truck
- soon designated SCP-1386 - did however prove

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:24.710
to be more difficult to contain than they
first imagined.

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:29.420
When a mobile task force attempted to engage
the truck in hopes of apprehending it, an

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:33.230
ear-splitting siren began to blast from the
truck’s undercarriage.

00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:36.840
This caused catastrophic inner-ear damage
to everyone involved.

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:41.220
Incidentally, it’s now believed that the
reason the ice cream truck engaged in this

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:46.080
defensive behavior had nothing to do with
the fact the mobile task force was armed,

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:49.050
but rather because of what they weren’t
carrying.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:54.620
It appears that SCP-1386 doesn’t turn on
its siren because of danger, but when it detects

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:58.430
that someone is approaching it who isn’t
carrying any money.

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:03.020
Eventually, the Foundation was able to trick
the ice cream truck into containment, luring

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:08.020
it into a fake, walled-off neighborhood where
it could drive its rounds constantly without

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:10.660
the risk of encountering civilians.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:15.460
All those who had previous encounters with
the ice cream truck were given amnestic treatment,

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:20.080
and SCP-1386 was finally officially contained.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:24.930
But while it had been taken off the streets,
the Foundation’s work was only just beginning:

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:28.090
It was time for research to commence.

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:32.009
The first key discoveries that aided in the
investigation involved the factors that are

00:05:32.009 --> 00:05:37.120
required for SCP-1386 to even serve its subjects
in the first place.

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:41.261
As the previously mentioned Mobile Task Force
learned, you need to approach the truck with

00:05:41.261 --> 00:05:46.550
at least twenty dollars in cash to be absolutely
sure that it won’t turn your ears inside

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:47.550
out.

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:51.820
The truck also proves to be extremely adept
at reading human emotions, and refuses to

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:54.570
serve anyone who doesn’t appear happy.

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:59.479
With these requirements now known, the Foundation
felt prepared to finally make some orders.

00:05:59.479 --> 00:06:02.759
First, they sent in a pair of Level Three
researchers.

00:06:02.759 --> 00:06:06.860
Each of them requested a delicious, cookies
and creme flavored smoothie.

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:10.500
The truck pushed both smoothies out of the
slot in its door, one marked with the letter

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:12.840
“M” and the other with the letter “G.”

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:17.340
A handwritten receipt with the price of $4.89
written on it.

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:21.210
They paid the price, and the transaction ended
without incident.

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:23.630
The smoothies were apparently pretty good,
too.

00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:29.340
Next, one of the researchers returned, perhaps
longing for another taste of SCP-1386’s

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:30.910
wonderful ice cream.

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:34.450
This time, he requested a Neapolitan ice cream
sandwich.

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:38.920
The truck rumbled for a moment, before dispensing
what seemed to be a ham and cheese sandwich

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:40.680
with slices of tomato.

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:45.699
However, upon taking a bite out of the sandwich,
the researcher found that this was actually

00:06:45.699 --> 00:06:51.430
just a perfect replica of a ham and cheese
sandwich made from Neapolitan ice cream.

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:55.750
The receipt released from the slot simply
said “April Fools!”, before the truck

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:59.199
drove away without even asking for any payment.

00:06:59.199 --> 00:07:04.039
The same researcher would return to the ice
cream truck one more time, this time requesting

00:07:04.039 --> 00:07:07.669
a single scoop of vanilla ice cream in a waffle
cone.

00:07:07.669 --> 00:07:13.009
It was provided to him without issue, and
he happily paid the 72 cents the truck requested

00:07:13.009 --> 00:07:14.169
in return.

00:07:14.169 --> 00:07:19.770
The next test wouldn’t go quite as swimmingly
- by which we mean, it caused a horrifying

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:20.919
death.

00:07:20.919 --> 00:07:24.970
This time, a slightly more senior researcher
wanted to perform a test on the ice cream

00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:25.970
truck.

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:29.509
He asked for a peach-flavored push pop, which
he received without issue.

00:07:29.509 --> 00:07:35.110
However, when he refused to pay the price
- an admittedly rather steep $16 - all hell

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:36.690
broke loose.

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:41.610
As he tried to walk away, the hatch opened
a full six feet, releasing its large, rusty,

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:43.770
metal trap around the senior researcher.

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:48.289
He was pulled into the truck, followed by
a horrific rumbling noise.

00:07:48.289 --> 00:07:54.979
Not long after, the slot began to spew a stream
of pink liquid for a solid five minutes, before

00:07:54.979 --> 00:07:56.440
driving away.

00:07:56.440 --> 00:08:00.639
This pink puree was later proven to be a genetic
match to the researcher.

00:08:00.639 --> 00:08:05.849
After this, the Foundation refused to allow
any other researchers to interact with SCP-1386.

00:08:05.849 --> 00:08:10.729
Only D-Class personnel would be permitted
to take part in tests..

00:08:10.729 --> 00:08:15.630
In contrast to the senior researcher’s horrifying
death, the D-Class personnel seemed to get

00:08:15.630 --> 00:08:18.599
along extremely well with SCP-1386.

00:08:18.599 --> 00:08:22.950
The first D-Class asked for a cherry popsicle
with nuts.

00:08:22.950 --> 00:08:27.930
The truck produced an unwrapped cherry popsicle
with nuts embedded in the ice, along with

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:32.000
a receipt reading, “$2.20 you’re nuts!”

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:36.390
The D-Class chuckled as he read the receipt,
and paid the truck without incident.

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:42.410
The second D-Class requested a more esoteric
treat - a "Caesar Salad flavor" Popsicle.

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:45.970
However, the ice cream truck isn’t one to
back down from a challenge.

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:51.090
It produced an off-green popsicle that tasted
like, quote, “lightly dressed lettuce with

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:52.690
a hint of croutons."

00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:57.040
The next D-Class ordered a Dark Chocolate
Fudge Pop, but wasn’t able to pay in exact

00:08:57.040 --> 00:08:58.040
change.

00:08:58.040 --> 00:09:02.090
He gave the truck two dollar bills, and was
given a carefully wrapped package with a crude

00:09:02.090 --> 00:09:04.230
drawing of US currency on the front.

00:09:04.230 --> 00:09:09.200
When the package was opened, he saw that it
contained the exact change he required, down

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:10.200
to the penny.

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:15.610
He made an official request to the Foundation
to keep the change, but his request was denied.

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:21.160
The Foundation then pushed its D-Class personnel
to ask for more complex constructions, just

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:24.740
to see what SCP-1386 was capable of.

00:09:24.740 --> 00:09:29.290
The next D-Class asked for a Kinder Surprise
Egg, the kind which are banned in the US due

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:31.800
to their history as a choking hazard.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:36.310
However, the ice cream truck didn’t have
a hard time constructing the egg, except this

00:09:36.310 --> 00:09:38.970
one was made out of ice cream rather than
chocolate.

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:44.100
It did seem beyond the truck’s capability
to create the toy inside, instead including

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:48.270
a small piece of paper reading, “I.O.U One
Toy.”

00:09:48.270 --> 00:09:51.090
The next interaction wasn’t quite as cordial.

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:56.700
The D-Class requested one cherry ice lolly,
one cherry ice pop, one cherry popsicle, and

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:59.320
one "cherry-flavored drink, frozen."

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:03.630
This resulted in the ice cream truck making
a horrifying noise, described as being “like

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:05.920
someone skinning a cat in reverse.”

00:10:05.920 --> 00:10:10.990
It then unceremoniously ejected the red ice,
causing it to shatter on the ground, before

00:10:10.990 --> 00:10:14.860
releasing a styrofoam cup filled with a frozen
green liquid.

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:19.820
This liquid was shown to contain huge quantities
of arsenic, but was thankfully impossible

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:24.320
to drink, on account of the fact its melting
point is so high that it’s impossible to

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:26.830
liquify with current technology.

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:32.410
And our current knowledge of SCP-1386’s
testing ends with its strangest story of all:

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:37.290
A non-verbal D-Class was instructed to write
his order on a piece of paper to pass to the

00:10:37.290 --> 00:10:41.360
truck, in hopes of seeing if it would respond
to written commands.

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:46.860
A slot opened up in the door a few inches
lower than the usual slot, and a thin, flesh-colored

00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:51.210
appendage slithered out, its hand a kind of
two-fingered pincer.

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:55.950
It took the note from the D-Class, and gave
him an ice cream cone in return.

00:10:55.950 --> 00:11:00.460
The D-Class was visibly disturbed by the hand
- saying it looked horrifying and smelled

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:01.460
like death.

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:06.150
He even refused to eat the ice cream, saying
that he’d lost his appetite.

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:11.580
But other D-Classes, capable of verbal articulation,
did not report any strange occurrences with

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:12.580
the hand.

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:16.900
They said that they found the hand to look
completely normal, and as time went on, they

00:11:16.900 --> 00:11:22.040
began to trust the ice cream truck with increasing
devotion - while their mistrust in the disturbed,

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:24.570
mute D-Class only grew.

00:11:24.570 --> 00:11:29.870
In the strangest twist of all, this D-Class
was later found dead in his cell from strangulation.

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:35.390
The D-Class was alone in his cell, and there
were no signs of forced entry.

00:11:35.390 --> 00:11:38.850
Perhaps he should have enjoyed his ice cream
while he still could...

00:11:38.850 --> 00:11:44.650
You know what they say: I scream, you scream,
we all scream for ice cream.

00:11:44.650 --> 00:11:52.130
And no ice cream is more scream-worthy than
the ones served up by SCP-1386.

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:58.621
Now check out “SCP-1861 - The Crew of the
HMS Wintersheimer” and “SCP-1730 - What

00:11:58.621 --> 00:12:03.260
Happened to Site-13?” for more things you
really wouldn’t want to get sucked into.

